      "problem": "An equilateral triangle has the same perimeter as a regular hexagon whose side is $5\\,mm.$ Find the length of the side of the triangle.",
      "worked_solution": "Since all the sides of the hexagon are equal, its perimeter is\n\n$$\np=6\\cdot 5=30\\,mm.\n$$\n\nLet $a$ be the side of the equilateral triangle. We know that our polygons have equal perimeters. Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =3a \\\\ 30 & =3a \\\\ 10 & =a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the length of the side is $10\\,mm.$",
